Task 5 — One Visualization
 Code:
 import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
df["sign"].value_counts().plot(kind="bar")
 plt.xlabel("Sign")
 plt.ylabel("Number of Observations")
 plt.title("Observation Count per Sign Class")
 plt.show()
 * One thing the chart reveals: It clearly reveals class counts at a glance (e.g., HELP has the most total observations with 3, while MEDICINE has the fewest with 1).
  * One thing the chart cannot reveal: It cannot reveal the underlying environmental or signer split within those counts (e.g., that all 3 HELP videos were recorded outdoors).



